  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "Sharing a common 凡 tongue 口"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a bucket or tube, now written as 筒. 口 (mouth) indicates that the character is only \"mouthed\", i.e. only used for its phonetic value."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "合會也。从𠔼从口。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形): a pipe — original form of 筒 (OC *doːŋ, *doːŋs, “pipe”). 口 was added later to mark the opening and prevent confusion.\nIn early forms, 同 (tóng) and 凡 were distinguished not by the presence of 口, but by symmetry: 同 (tóng) is symmetrical, while 凡 (fán) has its right stroke sweeping outward.\nPerhaps related to Tibetan སྡོང་བ (sdong ba, “to unite; to join”), Mizo intawng (inᴸ-tɔŋᴴ, “to meet together; to tally; to agree”), Mizo intawn (inᴸ-tɔn^F, “to meet together; to tally; to agree”). Unrelated to 叢 (OC *zloːŋ, “to collect; thicket”) (Schuessler, 2007)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "合會也。从𠔼从口。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "To join 會. Composed of 𠔼 and 口 'mouth'.",
